Source: UNHCR Refugee Population Statistics Database.

Everything under this directory comes from the UNHCR Refugee Population
Statistics Database, through UNHCR's public API at
https://api.unhcr.org/population/v1/.

UNHCR's methodology page (https://www.unhcr.org/refugee-statistics/methodology/)
says that, except where otherwise indicated, the datasets made available by
UNHCR on the UNHCR Refugee Population Statistics Database are licensed under
the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International Public License, and refers
to the Terms of Use for Datasets. Those terms, read on 2026-10-04 in the
Internet Archive's copy of 2026-09-21, require among other things:

  - attribution in the form "UNHCR Refugee Population Statistics Database"
    (item 3)
  - the URL of the Terms of Use for Datasets whenever the datasets are shared
    (item 4)
  - no statement or suggestion that UNHCR participates in, sponsors, approves
    or endorses the use (item 5)
  - no use of UNHCR's name or emblem (item 7)

They also say (item 6) that data provided by third parties may not be
redistributed without the consent of the original provider. The IDMC and
UNRWA series that UNHCR's API also serves are therefore not included here.
UNHCR may change the terms at any time (item 14).

This dataset is not made, sponsored or endorsed by UNHCR. It uses no UNHCR
logo or emblem; UNHCR's name appears only to identify the source.

The files under raw/<version>/unhcr/ are the API's files, byte for byte; each
version's MANIFEST.json records their URLs, sizes, sha256 and Last-Modified
(and also lists the third-party files fetched at the same time, which are not
here).

The Parquet under parquet/<version>/ was made from those files:

  - Year of the five data tables typed as an integer, the count columns as
    integers, and the "0" and "id" keys of the country list as integers;
    every other column is the text of the source
  - the "-" the CSVs write where there is no figure read as NULL
  - footnotes.csv taken from population.zip (the five zips carry the same file)
  - countries.json turned into one row per item, its keys as columns
  - column names, including the source's misspelling "Returned IDPss", and
    row order unchanged; no other value was changed

The code that fetches, checks and converts is in the repository this dataset
was built from (https://github.com/yuiseki/unhcr-refugee-stats) and does not
apply here.
